speechtext:
The expenditures of this
department a few years ago amounted to about $270,000. The insane patients have to be looked after; they are brought down and maintained by government grant in the New Westminster Asylum. Some of the items are as follows: freight and express charges, telegrams, telephones, postage, and so on, $4,520; legal expenses, $2,f>00; commission to the Royal North West Mounted Police, $2,000;
5 p.m. expenses in connection with export tax, $2,500; advertising mining regulations, etc., $5,000; printing and stationery, $5,000; travelling expenses of officials, $6,000; insane patients, $12,000; living allowances, $13,500; salaries, $66,980.
